  "packageHash": "TNxtG4ETXzc12sBAW0jW+qE+yEoTOK/RceGcDDJePVc2EJqx2oTyT6nuyGetFpVjZ/oQggwnmq40wyMOz6cH2A==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 259018,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard",
  "published": "2026-10-13T09:04:12.667Z",
  "readmeFile": "PackageReadme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Tool-result masking moves its boundary in steps, so a prepared request is the previous one plus the new messages between two steps and a provider prompt cache can reuse it. Adds the provider's finish reason and token counts to summarizer diagnostics, and a package icon. Fixes the tool name on a masked result, diagnostics for a compaction strategy that throws, and repeated summarizer requests after a failure.\n\nBehavior changes, with no signature changes: the default token budget is 40,000 instead of 25,000, so compaction starts at 32,000 tokens; prepared views mask further back at a step and differ from those of 1.1.0; the default placeholder of a masked result has a new, longer text; a call that starts while another call on the same context is still running throws InvalidOperationException; a recording call discards an exception thrown by a logger or meter listener; a failed summarizer call is not repeated while the history and the available tokens stay the same.\n\nKnown limits: summarization works with the built-in providers only, and a custom summarizer, compaction strategy, or token counter cannot be registered through the builder; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas and undercount pretty-printed JSON by 17% to 30% until the first provider report; one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.\n\nFull details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
